      "id": "DC_kwDOKrJqmc4A5_Ir",
      "body": "Update: Okay so I'm sure I could probably install from source and switch the gif but I love to do everything the hard way. As it stands I did a bunch of searching and dumped the filesystem and eventually concluded that the orca gif is probably in the rayhunter-daemon binary. I confirmed this using binwalker and I tried to patch the binary and replace it via netcat but all I did was disable rayhunter. Now I'm trying to figure out if I patched it wrong or the issue is something else.",
